@page "/gestures"
<PageTitle>Gestures & Movement Lab // The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<main class="gesture-lab">
    <a class="back-link" href="/hub">← RETURN TO THE HUB</a>
    <header class="hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">THE WORKSHOP // GESTURES RESEARCH</div>
        <h1>Intent becomes a pose.<br /><span>Evidence decides what happened.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Gestures is an engine-neutral .NET model for describing a physical procedure and evaluating its pose over time. It is one capability in a larger system—not a claim that animation alone can move a body through the physical world.</p>
        <div class="status">RESEARCH / CPU REFERENCE / RENDERER HANDOFF NOT YET INTEGRATED</div>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="eyebrow">01 // THE DATA PATH</div>
        <h2>A procedure is not a physical outcome.</h2>
        <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Gesture data flow">
            <article><b>01</b><strong>Authored procedure</strong><p>Keyframes and provider-defined named transforms describe the intended movement.</p></article>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            <article><b>02</b><strong>CPU evaluation</strong><p>The evaluator samples normalized time and returns an <code>EvaluatedPose</code>.</p></article>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            <article><b>03</b><strong>Rig / host adapter</strong><p>A consumer must map names, coordinate spaces, hierarchy, and root-offset policy.</p></article>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            <article><b>04</b><strong>Presentation</strong><p>Resolved representation can be presented only through a supported renderer contract.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">02 // WHAT THE POSE MEANS</div>
            <h2>Useful data, honest boundaries.</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>NormalizedProgress</strong> — the clamped point in the requested time interval.</li>
                <li><strong>IsComplete</strong> — the evaluator reached the time interval's end; not proof of success.</li>
                <li><strong>LocalTransforms</strong> — name-keyed local position, rotation, and scale values.</li>
                <li><strong>RootOffset</strong> — presentation/root-projection data, not authoritative world displacement.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="boundary">
            <div class="eyebrow">PHYSICS / DOMAIN OWNERSHIP</div>
            <h3>Reachability ≠ contact</h3>
            <p>Contact ≠ support. Support may slip, fail, or be released. A completed vehicle-boarding Gesture does not prove occupancy. Those outcomes must come from the owning physics or domain system.</p>
        </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="eyebrow">03 // IMPLEMENTATION STATUS</div>
        <h2>Current evidence, next seams.</h2>
        <div class="status-grid">
            <article><span class="state implemented">IMPLEMENTED ON REVIEW BRANCH</span><h3>CPU reference</h3><p>Engine-neutral pose evaluation, deterministic bounded variation, initial translation golden vectors, and test-backed soldier-movement and vehicle-boarding examples.</p></article>
            <article><span class="state pending">PENDING</span><h3>Host rig mapping</h3><p>No universal rig is assumed. A consumer must define the mapping and parent-transform composition.</p></article>
            <article><span class="state pending">PENDING</span><h3>Renderer pose contract</h3><p>The currently inspected Renderer frame accepts resolved draw commands; it does not expose a named-skeleton or evaluated-pose input slot.</p></article>
            <article><span class="state unmeasured">UNMEASURED</span><h3>GPU parity / crossover</h3><p>No CPU/GPU parity or workload crossover is claimed. Both require reference outputs and measured representative workloads.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section source-trail">
        <div class="eyebrow">04 // FOLLOW THE EVIDENCE</div>
        <h2>Inspect the work, not just the story.</h2>
        <p>The source branch is under review. The links below distinguish implementation evidence from proposals and the host integration plan.</p>
        <div class="links">
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/tree/work/planar-ik-reference" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gestures source branch ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/pull/10" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open review · PR #10 ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/blob/work/planar-ik-reference/docs/ROADMAP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Research roadmap ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/blob/work/planar-ik-reference/docs/RENDERER_POSE_HANDOFF_PROPOSAL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Renderer handoff proposal ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/WebPage/blob/development/docs/integrations/GESTURES_RENDERER_WEBPAGELLM_HANDOFF.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebPage integration brief ↗</a>
        </div>
    </section>
    <footer>Illustrative architecture only. This page does not run the .NET evaluator, simulate physics, or claim a live Gesture-to-Renderer adapter.</footer>
</main>

